{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "06TD", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F} = [U/R]$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\underline{\\xi} : \\underline{R}|_{\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda} \\to \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0004": "$U \\cong \\underline{R}|_{\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0006": "$TU \\to T\\mathcal{F} = T[U/R]$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{theorem-presentation-deformation-groupoid}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-RS-implies-S1-S2}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-minimal-versal}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{theorem-miniversal-object-existence}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{equation-bijective-orbits}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d76b0c99ec5064b7595ffcff99678c49323853dde6a63daec7ee9c462192b63a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:69ab66d8bb9de35167487cdda3cd58b65231a6d89aeed6f5f65f488ddf20453b", "source_text": "Part (1) follows immediately from the definitions.\nTo see part (2) set <MATH_0001>. Since <MATH_0002>\nhas a presentation it is a deformation category, see\nTheorem <REF_0001>.\nIn particular it satisfies (RS), (S1), and (S2), see\nLemma <REF_0002>.\nRecall that minimal versal formal objects are unique up to isomorphism, see\nLemma <REF_0003>.\nBy\nTheorem <REF_0004>\na minimal versal object induces a map\n<MATH_0003>\nsatisfying (<REF_0005>). Since\n<MATH_0004> over <MATH_0005>\nwe see that <MATH_0006> satisfies the property\nas stated in the lemma.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:76c7434a8b4d4237096ec7f24b3035a961cc35fe8eb336783adadd342a7c6853", "unit_id": "tag:06KN:proof"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "06TD", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal\nC_\\Lambda$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:3036a24565a93abf1c8c699c7b8492de873c6823e29841a4a645cbccf96ff9f3", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ccd8ff3823a96b5f05d73ac99d5abed7ab2eef66b8d0884a8b43250d7939e06c", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe quotient of a minimal prorepresentable groupoid in functors on <MATH_0001> does not admit autoequivalences which are not automorphisms.  To\nprove this, we first note the following lemma.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5d1e4de00d1f7aa9cc2e05911520cfa45c920f74442692c508f3999fb452afda", "unit_id": "tag:06TD:prose-0003"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "06TD", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$U: \\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda \\to \\textit{Sets}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\varphi : U \\to U$", "MATH_0003": "$d\\varphi : TU \\to TU$", "MATH_0004": "$\\varphi$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-surjective-morphism-prorepresentable-functor}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:8db9331666a87556414c23052289375bc77c444129a4d515b3cd72a6d1717265", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ef869dfeb821b787629dec88d73b8252422ab8b66187ed0eea23f60834a334b2", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a\nprorepresentable functor. Let <MATH_0002> be a morphism such\nthat <MATH_0003> is an isomorphism.  Then <MATH_0004> is an\nisomorphism.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d60e5bb71dcb46aaeaeb7c7019b1ca104d0cb0922416ea4317cc81dd3b7649d7", "unit_id": "tag:06KP:statement"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "06TD", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$U \\cong \\underline{R}|_{\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda}$", "MATH_0002": "$R \\in \\Ob(\\widehat{\\mathcal{C}}_\\Lambda)$", "MATH_0003": "$\\varphi$", "MATH_0004": "$\\underline{R} \\to \\underline{R}$", "MATH_0005": "$f: R \\to R$", "MATH_0006": "$\\widehat{\\mathcal{C}}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0007": "$f$", "MATH_0008": "$\\text{Der}_\\Lambda(R, k) \\to \\text{Der}_\\Lambda(R, k)$", "MATH_0009": "$f$", "MATH_0010": "$f$", "MATH_0011": "$\\underline{R}\n\\to \\underline{R}$", "MATH_0012": "$\\varphi : U \\to U$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{example-tangent-space-map-prorepresentable-functor}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-derivations-surjective}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-surjective-endo-noetherian-ring-is-iso}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:bb3381e1e5f71b264b4c81cd4b070b0b459c56a8776dc2f89d3a68ba3c3c9ec2", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e138f28b412d99f5223d140089e412d2edb8c1733bfda9eeae03b3a94f8cc444", "source_text": "If <MATH_0001> for some\n<MATH_0002>,\nthen completing <MATH_0003> gives a morphism <MATH_0004>.\nIf <MATH_0005> is the corresponding morphism in\n<MATH_0006>, then <MATH_0007> induces an isomorphism\n<MATH_0008>, see\nExample <REF_0001>.\nIn particular <MATH_0009> is a surjection by\nLemma <REF_0002>.\nAs a surjective endomorphism of a Noetherian ring is an isomorphism (see\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0003>)\nwe conclude <MATH_0010>, hence <MATH_0011>, hence <MATH_0012>\nis an isomorphism.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:33627110e584c4c1bae782b816b56e3840cb0bbfeba47e212b086f371211fe77", "unit_id": "tag:06KP:proof"}
